WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.300
Margaret is seventy-eight, and lives alone.

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.800
Wick cares for her through the screen she already watches.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:10.600
Her daughter Sarah opens the Wick family app, a simulated Alexa+ surface,

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.900
and enters the code on Margaret's Vega TV.

5
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.000
Nothing is shared until Margaret allows it.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.500
And when her week looks different, Wick asks her first.

7
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.000
Then Sarah just asks.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Agents on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore answer through Wick's MCP server, from counted facts only.

9
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:42.600
A ring at the door puts a card over her film: a picture, and one sentence from Amazon Nova.

10
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.800
One press asks Sarah to look, and her answer appears on screen.

11
00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.000
Sarah hands Wick an errand.

12
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.800
The agent arranges the visit and the note, asking before each step.

13
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:05.000
The note waits for a quiet cut in the film, and Margaret replies with one button.

14
00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:16.800
Outside Wick, the door still gets through, on Vega OS and Fire OS alike.

15
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.400
And Sarah's errand closes itself.

16
00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.600
Wick. Built for the person being cared for.
